# One half of a pair with `.gitignore`: the build context must not see what the
# tree does not carry anyway.
#
# Every name here matches at any depth, because what a build must not see —
# dependencies, build output, git's own directory, a worktree, and every `.env`
# (deploy.example.sh keeps its settings in .env.production; any .env.* holds
# APP_SECRET) — sits in a package as often as at the root.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.git
**/.git
# `.env` at any depth: `web/.env.local` is Vite's own convention, and a name
# that matches only at the root is exactly the one a build would carry.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
# A worktree is a second checkout, not content.
.worktree
server/data
